# __GAME__

A co-op game on [unified](https://github.com/FylmTM/godot-unified) (deterministic rollback netcode, Odin + Godot), started
from `uni init`: a copy of unified's `games/minimal_3d`, where 1–4 players move capsules and throw balls up. Make it
yours from here, starting with the design below (a draft skeleton: the game's rules, before its code), and read
`GUIDE.md` before writing gameplay: the patterns that survive prediction and rollback, and the gotchas by symptom.

```
./uni test --suite all # the sim tests and the game under headless Godot (uni.cmd on Windows)
./uni run              # play, in a window
./uni headless -- synctest --ticks 600 --window 8 # the sim without Godot (-- help: every mode)
./uni help             # every command
```

- `simulation/__GAME__/`: the deterministic sim (unified/src/sim/README.md: f32 only, no pointers in the state):
  `game.odin` (the Game and its tick), `state.odin` (State), `input.odin` (Input and the commands), `events.odin`,
  a file per part of the rules (`players.odin`, `balls.odin`) and `script.odin` (the scripted players of tests and
  headless runs).
- `simulation/headless/`: the headless binary (offline runs, sync-tests, benchmarks).
- `simulation/extension/`: the GDExtension: the sim run by unified's Godot integration (unified/src/godot/README.md):
  `input.odin` turns Godot's input into an Input, `frame.odin` the state into views.
- `simulation/tests/`: the standard scenarios and the determinism lint (`suite_test.odin`, which says how to pin a
  reference run), and the game's own rule tests.
- `game/`: the Godot side: scenes, views (each with a UnifiedView marker; `uni bake` indexes them into
  `unified_index.tres`) and scripts. GDScript reads the sim; input and commands are the only way in.
- `tools/`: this game's CLI (unified's public commands, plus the game's own).
- `unified/`: unified, as a git submodule. Local paths (a Godot install, the EOS SDK) go in a git-ignored `.env`.

## What to take from where

A game stays this shape: no menus or settings, one scene that starts a session. unified's other games
(`unified/games/`) show the rest; survivor's, drift's and friendslop's menus, settings and HUD panels (`game/app/`,
`game/ui/`) are their own, not a template:

- **Playing together:** the session's flags and `uni coop`. Direct (LAN) works as is (`--host-port`, `--join`,
  `uni coop --lan`); online (EOS lobbies and P2P: `--host-online`, `--join-code`) once the game passes
  `eos.lobby({})` to `godot.init` and `lobbies` to `modes.run` (drift's extension, survivor's headless main).
- **A physics World on a level with markers:** friendslop (3D: characters, joints, sensors), drift (2D on a plane).
- **Tables, handles, a view per entity, rule tests on `headless.Run`:** drift.
- **A population, a benchmark with `bench_prepare`, keyed rolls, a tuning variant:** survivor.
